<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCM_1ATM_0DEG_C> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> " The $\\textit{standard cubic metre}$ (scm) is a unit representing the amount of gas (such as natural gas) contained in a volume of one cubic metre at reference temperature and pressure conditions. As such, it is a measure of the actual amount of gas, not the volume of the gas. The reference conditions for standard cubic metre are 0 degrees Celsius and 101.325 kilopascals (kPa) of pressure. " .
<http://www.loa-cnr.it/ontologies/DOLCE-Lite.owl#stative> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An occurrence-type is stative or eventive according  to whether it holds of the mereological sum of two of its instances, i.e. if it is  cumulative or not. A sitting occurrence is stative since the sum of two sittings  is still a sitting occurrence."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
