<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/A_Stat> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> " The unit $\\textit{Statampere}$, symbol $statA$ is a unit in the category of Electric current. It is also known as statamperes. This unit is commonly used in the cgs unit system. $\\textit{Statampere (statA)}$ has a dimension of $I$ where $I$ is electric current. It can be converted to the corresponding standard SI unit $A$ by multiplying its value by a factor of 3.355641E-010. " .
