<http://www.loa-cnr.it/ontologies/DOLCE-Lite.owl#quality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Qualities can be seen as the basic entities we can  perceive or measure: shapes, colors, sizes, sounds, smells, as well as weights, lengths,  electrical charges... 'Quality' is often used as a synonymous of 'property', but this is  not the case in this upper ontology: qualities are particulars, properties are universals.  Qualities inhere to entities: every entity (including qualities themselves) comes with  certain qualities, which exist as long as the entity exists."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
