<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MassieuFunction> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The Massieu function, $\\Psi$, is defined as: $\\Psi = \\Psi (X_1, \\dots , X_i, Y_{i+1}, \\dots , Y_r  )$,  where for every system with degree of freedom $r$ one may choose $r$ variables, e.g. , to define a coordinate system, where $X$ and $Y$ are extensive and intensive variables, respectively, and where at least one extensive variable must be within this set in order to define the size of the system. The $(r + 1)^{th}$ variable,$\\Psi$ , is then called the Massieu function." .
