<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/PlanckFunction> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The $\\textit{Planck function}$ is used to compute the radiance emitted from objects that radiate like a perfect \"Black Body\". The inverse of the $\\textit{Planck Function}$ is used to find the $\\textit{Brightness Temperature}$ of an object. The precise formula for the Planck Function depends on whether the radiance is determined on a $\\textit{per unit wavelength}$ or a $\\textit{per unit frequency}$. In the ISO System of Quantities, $\\textit{Planck Function}$ is defined by the formula: $Y = -G/T$, where $G$ is Gibbs Energy and $T$ is thermodynamic temperature." .
