<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SH> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A shake is an informal unit of time equal to 10 nanoseconds. It has applications in nuclear physics, helping to conveniently express the timing of various events in a nuclear explosion. The typical time required for one step in the chain reaction (i.e. the typical time for each neutron to cause a fission event which releases more neutrons) is of order 1 shake, and the chain reaction is typically complete by 50 to 100 shakes."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
