<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_SHORT> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "<p>The short ton is a unit of mass equal to 2,000 pounds (907.18474 kg). In the United States it is often called simply ton without distinguishing it from the metric ton (tonne, 1,000 kilograms / 2,204.62262 pounds) or the long ton (2,240 pounds / 1,016.0469088 kilograms); rather, the other two are specifically noted. There are, however, some U.S. applications for which unspecified tons normally means long tons.</p>"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
