<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HR> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The hour (common symbol: h or h) is a unit of measurement of time. In modern usage, an hour comprises 60 minutes, or 3,600 seconds. It is approximately 1/24 of a mean solar day. An hour in the Universal Coordinated Time (UTC) time standard can include a negative or positive leap second, and may therefore have a duration of 3,599 or 3,601 seconds for adjustment purposes. Although it is not a standard defined by the International System of Units, the hour is a unit accepted for use with SI, represented by the symbol h."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
