<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/RatioOfSpecificHeatCapacities> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> " The specific heat ratio of a gas is the ratio of the specific heat at constant pressure, $c_p$, to the specific heat at constant volume, $c_V$. It is sometimes referred to as the $\\textit{adiabatic index}$, or the $\\textit{heat capacity ratio}$, or the $\\textit{isentropic expansion factor}$, or the $\\textit{adiabatic exponent}$, or the $\\textit{isentropic exponent}$. " .
