<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DYN> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> " In physics, the $dyne$ is a unit of force specified in the centimetre-gram-second (CGS) system of units. The $dyne$ is a unit of force specified in the centimetre-gram-second (CGS) system of units. One $dyne$ is equal to $\\SI{10}{\\micro\\newton}$. Equivalently, the $dyne$ is defined as 'the force required to accelerate a mass of one gram at a rate of one centimetre per square second'. A $\\textit{dyne per centimetre}$ is the unit traditionally used to measure surface tension. " .
