<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraBYTE> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The terabyte is a multiple of the unit byte for digital information. The prefix tera means 10^12 in the International System of Units (SI), and therefore 1 terabyte is 1000000000000bytes, or 1 trillion bytes, or 1000 gigabytes. 1 terabyte in binary prefixes is 0.9095 tebibytes, or 931.32 gibibytes. The unit symbol for the terabyte is TB or TByte, but not Tb (lower case b) which refers to terabit."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
