<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BIOT> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "\"Biot\" is another name for the abampere (aA), which is the basic electromagnetic unit of electric current in the emu-cgs (centimeter-gram-second) system of units. It is called after a French physicist, astronomer, and mathematician Jean-Baptiste Biot. One abampere is equal to ten amperes in the SI system of units. One abampere is the current, which produces a force of 2 dyne/cm between two infinitively long parallel wires that are 1 cm apart."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
