<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/StaticPressure> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "\"Static Pressure\" is the pressure at a nominated point in a fluid. Every point in a steadily flowing fluid, regardless of the fluid speed at that point, has its own static pressure $P$, dynamic pressure $q$, and total pressure $P_0$. The total pressure is the sum of the dynamic and static pressures, that is $P_0 = P + q$." .
