<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ReactivePower> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "\"Reactive Power\", for a linear two-terminal element or two-terminal circuit, under sinusoidal conditions, is the quantity equal to the product of the apparent power $S$ and the sine of the displacement angle $\\psi$. The absolute value of the reactive power is equal to the non-active power. The ISO (and SI) unit for reactive power is the voltampere. The special name $\\textit{var}$ and symbol $\\textit{var}$ are given in IEC 60027 1." .
