<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/AT-PER-M> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> " The  $\\textit{Ampere Turn per Metre}$ is the SI unit of magnetic field strength. One ampere per meter is equal to $\\pi/250$ oersteds (12.566 371 millioersteds) in CGS units. The ampere per meter is also the SI unit of \"magnetization\" in the sense of magnetic dipole moment per unit volume; in this context $1 A/m = 0.001 emu per cubic centimeter$. " .
