<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroFARAD> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The \"microfarad\" (symbolized $\\mu F$) is a unit of capacitance, equivalent to 0.000001 (10 to the -6th power) farad. The microfarad is a moderate unit of capacitance. In utility alternating-current (AC) and audio-frequency (AF) circuits, capacitors with values on the order of $1 \\mu F$ or more are common. At radio frequencies (RF), a smaller unit, the picofarad (pF), is often used." .
