<http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MolarEnergy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "\"Molar Energy\" is the total energy contained by a thermodynamic system. The unit is $$J/mol$$, also expressed as $$joule/mole$$,  or $$joules per mole$$. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. The quantity has the dimension of $$M \\cdot L^2 \\cdot  T^{-2} \\cdot N^{-1}$$ where $$M$$ is mass, $$L$$ is length, $$T$$ is time, and $$N$$ is amount of substance." .
